  "cleanText": "Solution home \n\t\tCapium 365\n\t\tCapium 365 (Accountant)\n\n### CAPIUM 365: Adding Transactions one at a time\n\n\t\t\tPrint\n\n\tModified on: Thu, 9 Oct, 2025 at 10:18 AM\n\n\t\tAdding Transactions one at a time\n\nNavigation: Capium 365 > Client > Books > + Transaction\n\n1. Go to Client > Books.\n\n2. Click on the \"+ Transaction\" button.\n\n3. Fill in the transaction details:\n\nTransaction Type: Choose between Income or Expense.\nSupplier: Select or add a supplier.\nDate: Set the transaction date. (Mandatory Field) \nTransaction Amount: Enter the amount for the transaction. (Mandatory Field) \nPayment Account: Select the relevant payment account or create a new account (Mandatory Field). Here you can only add transactions based on the bank entries. \nPayment Status: Mark as paid (if applicable).\nAccount Name: Assign the transaction to a specific account.\nReference: Enter a unique reference if needed.\nSource: Select the transaction source.\n4. Save and Exit\n\nSee screenshot below for reference:\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tDid you find it helpful?\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tYes\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tNo\n\nSend feedback\tSorry we couldn't be helpful. Help us improve this article with your feedback.",
